# Cartwright project rules

This codebase is a **Cartwright-engine store** — a single Next.js 16 + React 19 +
TypeScript app that runs as a corporate website, a webshop, or an agent-marketplace
depending on `brand.config.ts`. The full project briefing is in `.claude/CLAUDE.md`.

> **Designing this site? Read `DESIGN.md` first** — the design playbook: the three design
> paths (compose a look / mockup-first / Blank Canvas), built-ins inventory (three.js is
> already shipped — don't install it), taste rules, and screenshot self-verification.

> **See also** (same rules, other agents): `.cursor/rules/cartwright.mdc` (Cursor),
> `.github/copilot-instructions.md` (Copilot), `GEMINI.md` (Gemini), `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code).

> Cartwright is an open-source, AI-first Next.js + Stripe commerce engine. Scaffold one
> with `npx create-cartwright`. Source: https://github.com/Teloz1870/cartwright-template

## Run it & sign in (first time)

> **`--profile site` scaffold?** (`.cartwright/profile.json` says which profile you have.) There is no database, admin or login here — skip the first-run steps below: `pnpm dev` is the whole first run, `pnpm build` the whole production gate, and deploying needs no environment variables. Guide: `docs/simple-site.md`.

A fresh project is empty until the schema is created and the admin is seeded.
`npx create-cartwright` runs steps 1–2 for you and prints the admin login — if you scaffolded with it,
skip to step 3. Manual clone:

1. `pnpm install`
2. `pnpm db:setup` — creates the schema **and** seeds the admin + demo data; prints the admin **email +
   password** and writes them to **`.admin-credentials`** (gitignored). Auto-falls-back via the libSQL
   client if `prisma db push` hits the flaky Prisma 7.8 `Schema engine error:`.
3. `pnpm dev` (an agent: `pnpm dev:agent`, see "Start the dev server (agents)") → open
   **`/account/login`** → **Password** tab. Email = `brand.emails.admin`; password = the value in
   `.admin-credentials` (`cat .admin-credentials`). First login forces a change at `/admin/konto`,
   then `/admin/setup` opens.

Magic-link only appears once `RESEND_API_KEY` is set (dev link → `.mail-previews/`); until then password
is the only method, by design. Pre-set with `ADMIN_PASSWORD` before `db:setup`.

To go from booted to **designed** (apply a Voice/Skin via the REST tool surface, terminal-only), follow `.claude/CLAUDE.md` → "Your first 10 minutes".

## Start the dev server (agents)

Never assume `localhost:3000`: when port 3000 is taken, `next dev` moves on to 3001, 3002, ….
`pnpm dev:agent` is `pnpm dev` plus the URL Next actually chose, written with your
`brand.defaultLocale` path to `.cartwright/dev-url` (e.g. `http://localhost:3001/en`), and the PID
of that `next dev`, written to `.cartwright/dev-pid`. Next allows one `next dev` per project, so
while that PID is alive the block reuses its server and never starts a second one — even when the
URL does not answer yet (a compile, a restart). Only when the PID is dead or missing (a hard kill
leaves both files behind, and another app may take the port) does it delete both files and start
`pnpm dev:agent` in the background. Either way it polls the URL for a 200 with a bound — a cold
first compile takes 10–30 s:

```bash
SERVER_PID=$(cat .cartwright/dev-pid 2>/dev/null)  # the next dev an earlier call started
if ! kill -0 "$SERVER_PID" 2>/dev/null; then         # dead or missing: start a fresh one
  rm -f .cartwright/dev-url .cartwright/dev-pid      # a hard kill leaves both behind
  pnpm dev:agent > /tmp/cartwright-dev.log 2>&1 &
  DEV_PID=$!                                         # started here: yours to kill when done
  SERVER_PID=$DEV_PID
fi                                                   # alive: reuse it, even before it answers
for i in $(seq 90); do                               # bounded: 90 tries, then read the log
  kill -0 "$SERVER_PID" 2>/dev/null || break         # it exited: see below
  URL=$(cat .cartwright/dev-url 2>/dev/null) &&
    [ "$(curl -sL -m 60 -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' "$URL")" = 200 ] && break
  sleep 2
done
BASE=$(sed -E 's#^(https?://[^/]+).*#\1#' .cartwright/dev-url 2>/dev/null)  # e.g. http://localhost:3001
```

Every curl example in these rules uses `$BASE`. No 200 when the loop ends? If the block started the
server, read `/tmp/cartwright-dev.log`: "Another next dev server is already running" means one is up
that the block did not find (a plain `pnpm dev` writes no `.cartwright/dev-url`) — reuse the URL it
prints, or `kill` the PID it names. If it reused one, run the block again: it keeps waiting while
that PID lives and starts a fresh server once it is gone. (After a reboot another process can hold
that PID: if `ps -o args= -p "$(cat .cartwright/dev-pid)"` shows no `next dev`, delete both
`.cartwright/` files first.) Done? If the block started the server, `kill "$DEV_PID"` stops
`next dev` too and deletes both `.cartwright/` files; a server it reused is left running. If your
shell does not keep variables between calls, run the block again in each call — while its server
lives it only reuses it — or start `pnpm dev:agent` once with your tool's own background mode and
re-read `.cartwright/dev-url` in each call.

## This is NOT the Next.js you know

Next.js 16 has breaking changes vs. older training data. Read the relevant guide in
`node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing routing/rendering code.

## Modern web platform first

Default to native browser APIs over JS libraries:

- Modals/drawers → `<dialog>` + Popover API (`popover="auto"`/`"manual"`).
- SPA transitions → `document.startViewTransition`; cross-document → `@view-transition { navigation: auto }`.
- Responsive components → container queries (`@container`), not per-component media queries.
- State selectors → `:has()`, `:user-valid`, `:user-invalid`, `:state(...)`.
- Animation → CSS-only where possible (`@starting-style`). Site-wide motion: see `.claude/CLAUDE.md` → "Motion & animation" (motionEffects presets, three-scenes plugin, or the SSR-safe GSAP recipe).
- Long sync work → `scheduler.yield()` to protect INP.
- New color decisions → `oklch()`/`lch()` (don't rename existing `--color-sol-*` tokens).

## Structured data is mandatory

Every AI-citable page ships `<JsonLd>` markup (SSR only; helper at `components/JsonLd.tsx`).
Shipped: Organization, Product, Offer, BreadcrumbList, AggregateRating, BlogPosting, FAQPage,
and SoftwareApplication (on `/built-with-cartwright`, gated by `brand.features.cartwrightBadge`).
Never put JSON-LD in `"use client"` components.

## Feature flags

Subsystems live behind `brand.features.*` in `brand.config.ts`; the authoritative list is
`lib/feature-flags/manifest.ts`. New features ship default-off — flip on staging, then promote.

## File map

- `brand.config.ts` — single source of truth for brand, mode, flags, policies.
- `themes/<slug>.css` — color palette per shop.
- `components/JsonLd.tsx` — structured data.
- `lib/feature-flags/manifest.ts` — every feature flag (compile-enforced).
- `lib/plugins/` + `plugins/` — plugin contract (`cartwright-plugin-v1`) + in-repo plugins (first: `plugins/phone-widget/`).
- `app/admin/` — admin UI; `lib/ai/prompts/<slug>.ts` — AI assistant prompt per shop.
- `designs/blank/` — the **Blank Canvas** pack: rewrite its header/footer/homepage freely for a fully unique design while all backend (cart, checkout, admin, AI tools, SEO) keeps working. Guide: `AGENTS.md` → "Blank canvas — build a design from scratch".

## Capturing leads

Don't build an inquiry table — one ships. `Lead` (`prisma/schema.prisma`) ←
`POST /api/inquiries` → `/admin/leads`. The no-DB site profile uses
`app/api/inquiries/route.static.ts`, which mails the owner instead.

Custom forms (calculators, quote wizards) send two extra fields: `source`
(which form, ≤64 chars) and `data` (a JSON object of whatever you collected,
≤50 keys / ≤4 KB). Keys OUTSIDE `data` are stripped by Zod, so put custom
fields inside it. Over a cap is a `400` with its own code, never a silent
truncation.

Adding columns to `Lead` requires `pnpm db:push` before the code runs — Prisma
`INSERT … RETURNING` names every column, so an unmigrated DB fails on write as
well as read.

## Don't

- Don't put credentials in tracked files (`.env.local`, `.mcp.json`, `i18nexus.json` are gitignored).
- Don't ship a new feature default-on without a feature flag.
- Don't rename `--color-*` CSS tokens once products reference them.
- Don't reach for an npm library when a Baseline-2024+ browser API does the same thing.
